    "text": "The model tracks vaccinated people in the V compartment. Their rate of change follows the paper's equation dV/dt = πS − (θ + μ)V. The contact rate beta does not appear in this equation, but raising beta increases infections elsewhere and pulls people out of the protected group. When beta is doubled to 0.00000155, the peak of vaccinated people within 38 years falls by more than 3,000,000. This agrees with the paper's sensitivity result that beta is one of the most important factors."
  },
